# Packed lookup tables for the literal M22 word certificates

Each natural stores 128 entries, with 13 bits per entry. Small named blocks
keep kernel reduction from repeatedly copying a large lookup expression.
These are untrusted numerical data. `Action` proves equality with the published
ATLAS cycle products, and subsequent certificates check all word operations.

Generated by `generate_tables.py` from the retained ATLAS files. Attribution
and the original data remain in the sibling `source/` directory; no new ATLAS
code is copied. Mathematical application: Aschbacher–Smith I.1.3(4).
-/

